Runtime: Adapter — Integration Bridge

Purpose:
  Turns `.sdd` specifications (gates, state, policies) into enforced
  runtime checks via claude-code hooks (PostToolUse[Edit/Write], PreCommit)
  and claude-mem stores (observation persistence, context recall).

  This is the missing piece that converts `.sdd` from spec-only (advisory)
  into a runtime-enforced system.

Principles:
  Spec-first brain, runtime-first body.
  `.sdd` models declare intent; adapter enforces at tool-execution boundary.
  Adapter is zero-dependency core; external integrations are optional plugins.
  All enforcement decisions are observable (OBS1-20).
  Failure is fail-open in observe mode; fail-closed in enforce mode.

AdapterComponents:
  HookBridge:
    definition: Bidirectional bridge between .sdd gates and claude-code hooks
    responsibility: Translate .sdd security controls into claude-code hook exit codes
    lifecycle:
      on: PostToolUse[Write/Edit]
      action: read .sdd/security/controls.sdd patterns
      action: match against tool input
      action: if match and L-level >= project threshold -> exit 2 (block)
      action: if match and L-level < threshold -> log OBS (warn mode)
      output: OBS1-20 event with gate decision, pattern matched, file, severity

  GateRuntime:
    definition: Executes .sdd/gates/*.sdd decisions at tool-execution time
    responsibility: Read gate schema, evaluate condition, enforce threshold
    lifecycle:
      on: pre-tool-execution
      action: load gate from .sdd/gates/<type>.sdd
      action: evaluate Condition against tool context
      action: compare result to Threshold
      action: emit GateDecision event
      output: PASS -> allow | FAIL -> block + emit OBS

  MemoryBridge:
    definition: Connects .sdd/runtime/memory-model.sdd to claude-mem stores
    responsibility: Route observations to claude-mem persistence; recall context on demand
    lifecycle:
      on: PostToolUse (all tools)
      action: sanitize observation (L0 sanitization step)
      action: SHA-256 content-hash dedup
      action: store to claude-mem SQLite + ChromaDB
      on: UserPromptSubmit
      action: load context from claude-mem (tier routing, ~52% token savings)
      action: inject into context window

  EventBridge:
    definition: Maps .sdd/runtime/events.sdd to claude-code hook events
    responsibility: Emit OBS1-20 observations for all gate decisions, tool calls, memory operations
    lifecycle:
      on: every hook event
      action: create Observation record
      action: log to .sdd/runtime/events.sdd append-only log
      output: OBS1-20 observability event

GateExecution:
  flow:
    claude-code PostToolUse[Edit] ->
      HookBridge reads .sdd/security/controls.sdd ->
      Pattern match against file content ->
      L-level determination from .sdd/security/levels.sdd ->
      Project security level from PROJECT.sdd ->
      if L-level >= project_threshold: exit 2 (block) ->
      else: log OBS12 security_gate_warned ->
      claude continues

  observe_vs_enforce:
    OBSERVE: warnings logged, tool proceeds, OBS emitted
    ENFORCE: exit 2 on HIGH/CRITICAL, blocks tool call entirely

  configuration:
    source: PROJECT.sdd SecurityLevel (L0-L5)
    source: .sdd/security/controls.sdd L-level per pattern
    source: .sdd/security/levels.sdd decision thresholds
    default: ENFORCE for L4+Critical, OBSERVE for L1-L3

MemoryObservationFlow:
  store:
    sanitize: L0 sanitization strip (prompt-injection prevention)
    dedup: SHA-256 content-hash, ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    tier: promote based on .sdd/runtime/memory-consolidation.sdd rules (100 events -> 3 decisions + 1 skill)
    persist: claude-mem SQLite (hot) + ChromaDB (semantic) + SHA-256 (dedup)

  recall:
    tier_route: filter -> ChromaDB semantic -> FTS5 fallback
    recency_gate: 90-day window (configurable)
    token_budget: progressive disclosure (metadata first, instructions on activate, resources on demand)
    inject: sanitized, deduplicated, tier-routed context into claude-code session

Migrations:
  pattern: 49 idempotent migrations from claude-mem SessionStore.ts
  rule: migrations tracked in .sdd/runtime/migrations.sdd
  rule: crash-safe — re-running migration is safe
  rule: version recorded in runtime state DB

IntegrationPoints:
  claude-code:
    hooks: PostToolUse[Edit/Write], PreCommit, SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit
    configuration: .clauderc.json or settings.json hook definitions
    plugin: .claude-plugin/adapter.json (optional)

  claude-mem:
    daemon: per-user port (default 37700 + uid % 100)
    API: REST endpoints for observation store/recall
    database: SQLite (metadata) + ChromaDB (embeddings) + SHA-256 (dedup)
    config: CLAUDE_MEM_TIER_ROUTING_ENABLED, CLAUDE_MEM_SANITIZATION_ENABLED

  security-review:
    engine: claudecode/github_action_audit.py
    integration: .sdd review-stage plugin, invoked from CR gate
    output: findings -> .sdd/reviews/<task>/security-findings.sdd
    filter: findings_filter.py two-stage (hard-regex + Claude API confidence)

Rules:
  [ADAPTER1] Adapter MUST translate .sdd gate schema into claude-code hook exit codes.
  [ADAPTER2] Adapter MUST NOT modify .sdd specification files — it only reads them.
  [ADAPTER3] In OBSERVE mode, adapter MUST emit OBS1-20 events for all gate decisions.
  [ADAPTER4] In ENFORCE mode, adapter MUST exit non-zero on gate failure for L-level >= project threshold.
  [ADAPTER5] All memory observations MUST pass through sanitization before storage.
  [ADAPTER6] Duplicate observations MUST be suppressed via SHA-256 content-hash dedup.
  [ADAPTER7] Memory recall MUST use tier routing (filter → semantic → FTS5 fallback).
  [ADAPTER8] Adapter MUST persist runtime state in DB, not RAM.
  [ADAPTER9] Adapter MUST support crash recovery — resume from last checkpoint.
  [ADAPTER10] Migration execution MUST be idempotent and crash-safe.
  [ADAPTER11] Adapter MUST emit audit trail for every gate decision (GateDecision event).
  [ADAPTER12] Adapter MUST NOT hard-code model versions — read from .sdd standards.
  [ADAPTER13] Adapter MUST NOT log secrets — scrub ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN from logs.
  [ADAPTER14] External dependencies (claude-code, claude-mem) MUST be version-pinned, not @latest.
  [ADAPTER15] Adapter MUST support graceful degradation if external dependency is unavailable.

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Gates: @../gates/INDEX.sdd
  Security: @../gates/security.sdd
  Security Levels: @../security/levels.sdd
  Events: @events.sdd
  Memory Model: @memory-model.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Protocol: @../protocol/ROOT.sdd

